---
// BaseLayout's own theme-init script (colorScheme="auto") reads localStorage
// `at-theme`, falling back to the OS preference, and writes `data-theme`
// right before its `<slot name="head" />` — see BaseLayout.astro. Passing
// this component into that slot runs it straight after, so it only has to
// override the "nothing stored yet" case: a first visit lands on the dark
// stage on any OS, while a stored preference (the footer toggle) still wins.
---

<script is:inline>
  if (!localStorage.getItem("at-theme")) {
    document.documentElement.dataset.theme = "dark";
  }
</script>
